From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: Add Apple D2186 PMIC ADC driver

Add an IIO ADC driver for the 12-bit housekeeping ADC inside the Dialog
D2186 PMIC found on Apple A8 devices such as the iPod touch 6 (N102).

The ADC attaches as a child of the Apple I2C PMIC simple-mfd regmap and
performs serialized, bounded polled conversions without enabling or
touching the PMU event interrupt registers:

- Writing (channel & 0x1f) | BIT(7) to 0x500 starts a conversion; bit 7
  clears when the conversion completes (polled at 1 ms with a 50 ms
  timeout).
- Result bytes at 0x502..0x503 encode a 12-bit value as
  (reg[0x502] & 0x0f) | (reg[0x503] << 4). Bit 7 of 0x502 flags an
  invalid/overrange reading on channel 9 (ibus).
- Channels 0 (vcc_main) and 4 (vbat) measure 2500..5000 mV
  (offset 4096, scale 2500 / 4096 mV).
- Channel 15 (vbus) measures 0..5500 mV (scale 5500 / 4096 mV).
- Channel 1 (ich) measures charger output current at 0..1000 mA
  (scale 1000 / 4096 mA).
- Channel 2 (tbat) measures a 10 kOhm NTC thermistor driven at 50 uA
  (Vntc = raw * 2500 / 4096 mV, Rntc = Vntc * 20000 Ohm) converted to
  millidegrees Celsius via the 34-point -40..125 C lookup table.
- Channel 9 (ibus) converts raw counts using the PMIC's factory two-point
  calibration registers at 0x51d..0x520, die-temperature trim at 0x4a2
  (channel 0x14), and 2D VBUS/temperature Ron compensation table.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
